<title>USA: TABLE - ACNielsen Corp Q2 net rises.</title>
<headline>TABLE - ACNielsen Corp Q2 net rises.</headline>
<dateline>STAMFORD, Conn. 1997-07-17</dateline>
<text>
<p>Condensed Statements of Earnings</p>
<p>			 (in millions, except per share amounts)</p>
<p>				 For the Quarters Ended June 30,</p>
<p>					 1997		 1996</p>
<p> Operating Revenue	    $  356.3	  $  336.9</p>
<p> Operating Costs		   192.0	     176.3</p>
<p>Selling &amp; Administrative</p>
<p>  Expenses			   122.5	     126.8</p>
<p> Depreciation &amp; Amortization    23.1		22.8</p>
<p> Operating Income		   18.7		11.0</p>
<p>Non-Operating Income</p>
<p>  (Expense), Net		     0.3	     (1.0)</p>
<p>Income Before Income</p>
<p>  Tax Provision		     19.0		10.0</p>
<p> Income Tax Provision (a)	(8.8)	     (8.3)</p>
<p> Net Income			   10.2		 1.7</p>
<p>Net Income Per Share</p>
<p>  of Common Stock (b)	     0.18		0.03</p>
<p>Average Number of</p>
<p>  Shares Outstanding (b)	  57.0		56.7</p>
<p>				For the Six Months Ended June 30,</p>
<p>					1997		1996</p>
<p> Operating Revenue	  $  681.1	  $  644.2</p>
<p> Operating Costs		 382.5	     355.5</p>
<p>Selling &amp; Administrative</p>
<p>  Expenses			 242.2	     249.1</p>
<p> Depreciation &amp; Amortization  46.9		47.3</p>
<p> Operating Income (Loss)	 9.5	     (7.7)</p>
<p> Non-Operating Income, Net     1.9		 0.2</p>
<p>Income (Loss) Before Income</p>
<p>  Tax Provision		   11.4	     (7.5)</p>
<p> Income Tax Provision (a)    (5.3)	     (9.9)</p>
<p> Net Income (Loss)		 6.1	    (17.4)</p>
<p>Net Income (Loss) Per Share</p>
<p>  of Common Stock (b)	   0.11	    (0.31)</p>
<p>Average Number of</p>
<p>  Shares Outstanding (b)	57.0		56.6</p>
<p>NOTE: (a) The tax provision for the quarter ended June 30, 1996 was calculated on a separate-company basis.  For the year ended December 31, 1996, the Company recorded a tax provision at a 48% effective rate, with the adjustment recorded on a year-to-date basis in the third quarter.  Utilizing a 48% effective rate for the quarter ended June 30, 1996 would have resulted in a net income of $5.2 million, or $0.09 per share.</p>
<p>(b) For the period prior to November 1, 1996, the computation is based on the average number of shares of D&amp;B Common Stock outstanding, adjusted for the one for three distribution ratio.</p>
<p>-- New York Newsdesk 212 859-1610</p>
